00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Sky High is a 2005 American superhero comedy film directed by Mike Mitchell, and written by
Paul Hernandez, and Kim Possible creators Bob Schooley and Mark McCorkle.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
The film stars Kelly Preston, Michael Angarano, Danielle
Panabaker, Mary Elizabeth Winstead and Kurt Russell.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
It follows Will Stronghold (Angarano), the son of two superheroes, who is
enrolled in an airborne high school for teenage superheroes.

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
As his dormant superpowers manifest, he struggles to maintain his relationships with his old friends,
learns of a threat from a mysterious supervillain, and searches for the girl of his dreams.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film was theatrically released by Buena Vista Pictures Distribution on July 29, 2005, and
grossed $86.4 million worldwide against a production budget of $35 million.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and audiences during its
original theatrical run and has since been recognized as a cult film.

16
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film explores themes of high school,
friendship, mission, superhero, loyalty.

17
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:36,000
The tone is lighthearted.
